Design for Upgrading (DfU) is a design tool which mainly focuses on enhancing the functionality of products and physical suitability for the ease of upgrade. Upgradability of the products helps in reducing natural-resource depletion, used-product disposal, and CO2 emissions. The upgradeable product design helps to extend the lifespan of the product. There are two methods for this strategy as follows:

•	Upgrade by replacing components with new and higher quality components
•	Upgrade through adding components or modifying the structure of the product